-- title:
--   Every element of the crossing model is a + bU with a,b invariant
-- statement:
--   Let $W$ be a commutative ring and $\pi \in W$. Write $R_\pi$ for the crossing model `UVCrossingModel W π`, namely the quotient of the ring of formal power series in two variables $\mathrm{MvPowerSeries}\,(\mathrm{Fin}\ 2)\ W$ by the ideal generated by $X_0 X_1 - C(\pi)$, and let `crossingSwap π` be the ring automorphism of $R_\pi$ induced by interchanging the two variables (the swap preserves the ideal, so it descends to the quotient). The subring `fixedSubring π` is by definition the locus where this automorphism agrees with the identity map, i.e. the subring of invariants. The theorem asserts that for every $x \in R_\pi$ there exist $a, b \in R_\pi$, both lying in `fixedSubring π`, such that $x = a + b \cdot U \pi$, where $U \pi$ denotes the image of the first variable in $R_\pi$. Thus $R_\pi$ is generated by $1$ and $U \pi$ as a module over its subring of invariants; no hypothesis on $W$ or $\pi$ beyond commutativity is imposed, and no uniqueness of the pair $(a,b)$, nor freeness of $\{1, U\pi\}$, is claimed.
--
--   This is the module-theoretic form of the statement that the local crossing model $W[[u,v]]/(uv-\pi)$ is a double cover of its branch-exchange invariants, the algebraic shadow of the Atkin–Lehner type involution interchanging the two branches at a crossing point of a modular curve in characteristic dividing the level. It is used in the analysis of the invariant subring and of the structure of $R_\pi$ over it, for instance in the identifications of $R_\pi$ with a quotient of a polynomial ring by a quadratic ([`ModularCurve.UVCrossingModel.exists_ringEquiv_adjoinRoot`](thm.html#ModularCurve.UVCrossingModel.exists_ringEquiv_adjoinRoot) and its completeness variant) and in the length–rank comparison [`ModularCurve.UVCrossingModel.exists_mul_length_eq_mul_finrank_of_ne_bot_of_const_notMem`](thm.html#ModularCurve.UVCrossingModel.exists_mul_length_eq_mul_finrank_of_ne_bot_of_const_notMem).
